---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/animals.css';
import { translationsFor } from '../../i18n/routes';
---
<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Exotic Animals - Reptiles for Sale | NS Reptiles, Novi Sad"
  description="Healthy reptiles for sale - bearded dragons, leopard geckos, ball pythons, corn snakes and tarantulas. NS Reptiles breeder, Novi Sad."
  path="/en/animals.html"
  ogTitle="Exotic Animals - Reptiles for Sale | NS Reptiles"
  ogDescription="Healthy bearded dragons, geckos, pythons and tarantulas from NS Reptiles breeder, Novi Sad."
  active="animals"
  translations={translationsFor("/en/animals.html")}
>
<section class="page-head">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">Animals</div>
        <h1>Exotic animals</h1>
        <p>
          Healthy, properly fed reptiles ready for a new home - bred by us or
          sourced from trusted breeders in Serbia and the region.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="intro">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="intro-box">
          <div class="eyebrow">Our offer</div>
          <p>
            At <strong>NS Reptiles</strong> breeder, we work exclusively with
            species we have personally bred or sourced from trusted breeders. For
            each species, we have prepared a detailed guide with equipment and
            care recommendations, so your new pet has the right conditions from
            day one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="zoo">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="pills">
          <button class="pill" data-target="gusteri">Lizards</button>
          <button class="pill" data-target="zmije">Snakes</button>
          <button class="pill" data-target="tarantule">Tarantulas</button>
        </div>

        <!-- LIZARDS -->
        <div class="cat-block" id="cat-gusteri">
          <div class="cat-title">
            <h2>Lizards</h2>
            <span class="count">5 species</span><span class="line"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="zgrid">
            <a class="zcard" href="#">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <span class="zbadge">For beginners</span>
                <img src="/style/img/gallery/2.jpg" alt="Bearded dragon">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Pogona vitticeps</div>
                <h3>Bearded dragon</h3>
                <p>
                  One of the most popular lizard species and extremely suitable
                  for beginners. Intelligent and remarkably friendly towards
                  people.
                </p>
                <span class="zlink">View species
                  <span class="arr"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span></span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="zcard" href="#">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <span class="zbadge">For beginners</span>
                <img src="/style/img/gallery/3.jpg" alt="Leopard gecko">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Eublepharis macularius</div>
                <h3>Leopard gecko</h3>
                <p>
                  The most common gecko species in our region and an ideal pet
                  for beginners. Easy to maintain, calm and rarely bites.
                </p>
                <span class="zlink">View species
                  <span class="arr"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span></span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="zcard" href="#">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <img src="/style/img/gallery/13.jpg" alt="Chinese water dragon">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Physignathus cocincinus</div>
                <h3>Chinese water dragon</h3>
                <p>
                  An affectionate and calm lizard that tames easily, resembling
                  an iguana in appearance. Requires a spacious terrarium with
                  plenty of branches.
                </p>
                <span class="zlink">View species
                  <span class="arr"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span></span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="zcard" href="#">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <span class="zbadge">For beginners</span>
                <img src="/style/img/gallery/10.jpg" alt="African fat-tailed gecko">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Hemitheconyx caudicinctus</div>
                <h3>African fat-tailed gecko</h3>
                <p>
                  Not as popular as leopard geckos, but an equally good choice
                  for beginners. They stay relatively small and don't require
                  demanding care.
                </p>
                <span class="zlink">View species
                  <span class="arr"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span></span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="zcard" href="#">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <img src="/style/img/gallery/14.jpg" alt="Crested gecko">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Rhacodactylus ciliatus</div>
                <h3>Crested gecko</h3>
                <p>
                  A popular choice due to its small size, attractive appearance
                  and docile nature. It's nocturnal and doesn't need a heat lamp
                  at room temperature.
                </p>
                <span class="zlink">View species
                  <span class="arr"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span></span>
              </div>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SNAKES -->
        <div class="cat-block" id="cat-zmije">
          <div class="cat-title">
            <h2>Snakes</h2>
            <span class="count">2 species</span><span class="line"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="zgrid">
            <a class="zcard" href="#">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <span class="zbadge">For beginners</span>
                <img src="/style/img/gallery/7.jpg" alt="Ball python">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Python regius</div>
                <h3>Ball python</h3>
                <p>
                  An excellent choice for beginners among snake owners. They
                  usually grow up to 150 cm, are quite docile and easy to
                  handle.
                </p>
                <span class="zlink">View species
                  <span class="arr"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span></span>
              </div>
            </a>
            <a class="zcard" href="#">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <span class="zbadge">For beginners</span>
                <img src="/style/img/gallery/9.jpg" alt="Corn snake">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Pantherophis guttatus</div>
                <h3>Corn snake</h3>
                <p>
                  One of the most popular species. Requires a simple terrarium
                  and conditions that are easy to provide. Grows from 1.2 m to
                  1.6 m.
                </p>
                <span class="zlink">View species
                  <span class="arr"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span></span>
              </div>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- TARANTULAS -->
        <div class="cat-block" id="cat-tarantule">
          <div class="cat-title">
            <h2>Tarantulas</h2>
            <span class="count">5 species</span><span class="line"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="zgrid">
            <div class="zcard">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <img src="/style/img/tarantule/davus-pentaloris.png" alt="Guatemalan tiger rump tarantula">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Davus pentaloris</div>
                <h3>Guatemalan tiger rump tarantula</h3>
                <p>
                  A calm and docile tarantula ideal for beginners. Known for its
                  beautiful tiger-orange markings on the abdomen.
                </p>
                              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="zcard">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <img src="/style/img/tarantule/phormictopus-auratus.png" alt="Cuban gold tarantula">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Phormictopus auratus</div>
                <h3>Cuban gold tarantula</h3>
                <p>
                  An attractive tarantula from Cuba known for its golden-bronze
                  sheen. An active species with an impressive appearance.
                </p>
                              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="zcard">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <img src="/style/img/tarantule/acanthoscurria-geniculata.png" alt="Brazilian whiteknee tarantula">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Acanthoscurria geniculata</div>
                <h3>Brazilian whiteknee tarantula</h3>
                <p>
                  An imposing tarantula with white stripes on its legs. An
                  active and fast-growing species, popular among enthusiasts.
                </p>
                              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="zcard">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <img src="/style/img/tarantule/brachypelma-boehmei.png" alt="Mexican fireleg tarantula">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Brachypelma boehmei</div>
                <h3>Mexican fireleg tarantula</h3>
                <p>
                  A beautiful tarantula with bright red-orange legs. A calm
                  species, great for beginners.
                </p>
                              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="zcard">
              <div class="zcard-img">
                <img src="/style/img/tarantule/brachypelma-emilia.png" alt="Mexican redleg tarantula">
              </div>
              <div class="zcard-body">
                <div class="lat">Brachypelma emilia</div>
                <h3>Mexican redleg tarantula</h3>
                <p>
                  A classic Mexican tarantula with distinctive black and red
                  patterns. A calm and long-lived species.
                </p>
                              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STARTER BANNER -->
        <div class="starter">
          <div class="starter-txt">
            <h3>Complete starter kits</h3>
            <p>
              With every animal, we also offer ready-made starter kits -
              terrarium, lighting, heating, substrate and decoration, all
              tailored to the specific species. Ideal if you're just starting
              out.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a href="/en/" class="btn">Browse kits</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="section faq">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head reveal" style="text-align: center; max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto 46px">
          <div class="eyebrow center" style="justify-content: center">Frequently asked questions</div>
          <h2 class="sec-title">All about <b>reptiles</b></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list reveal">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q">
              Are reptiles good pets for beginners?<span class="ic">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Yes, many reptiles are excellent for beginners. Leopard geckos,
                crested geckos and bearded dragons are among the easiest to
                keep. They require less daily attention than dogs or cats, but
                do need proper equipment - a terrarium of appropriate size,
                heating, UVB lighting and a suitable diet.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q">
              How often should reptiles be fed?<span class="ic">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Juveniles are generally fed daily, while adults eat 2-4 times a
                week depending on the species. Bearded dragons eat every day
                (salad and insects), ball pythons once every 7-14 days, and
                leopard geckos every other day. Always dust food with calcium.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q">
              Do reptiles bond with their owners?<span class="ic">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Reptiles don't express emotions like mammals, but they do get
                used to contact with their owner and become calm during
                handling. Bearded dragons are particularly known for their
                tolerance and enjoyment of contact. Regular gentle handling from
                a young age helps.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q">
              What is the best first reptile?<span class="ic">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Leopard gecko - calm, eats insects, lives 15-20 years. Bearded
                dragon - social, omnivore, great for families. Crested gecko -
                doesn't need a heat lamp at room temperature and feeds on a
                ready-made mix.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q">
              How long do reptiles live?<span class="ic">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>
                Lifespan varies by species: leopard gecko 15-20 years, bearded
                dragon 8-12, ball python 20-30, corn snake 15-20, and tortoises
                can live 50+ years. Proper care and diet directly affect
                lifespan.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="zcta">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="justify-content: center">
          Interested?
        </div>
        <h2>Find your <b>perfect pet</b></h2>
        <p>
          Let us know which species you're interested in - we'll be happy to
          advise you on care, equipment and availability.
        </p>
        <div class="zcta-btns">
          <a href="https://wa.me/381693301474" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn" style="background: #fff; color: var(--green-dark)">WhatsApp</a>
          <a href="tel:+381693301474" class="btn btn-light">Call us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

<script is:inline slot="after">
      // pills scroll to category
      document.querySelectorAll('.pill').forEach((p) =>
        p.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const el = document.getElementById('cat-' + p.dataset.target);
          if (!el) return;
          const y =
            el.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - 150;
          window.scrollTo({ top: y, behavior: 'smooth' });
        }),
      );
    </script>
</Base>
